   "title": "How to use · tested on RTX 3060",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use\n\n1. **Step 1** — models are set (int8 = best fit for 12 GB).\n2. **Step 2** — size. Default **4 MP = 2048×2048** (Qwen 2.1's native 2K). 1 MP = 1024×1024.\n3. **Step 3** — write your prompt. cfg stays **1** (negative prompt is unused at cfg 1).\n4. **Run.** QUALITY is on; TURBO is bypassed. To switch: click a group title → **Ctrl+B**.\n\n## Tested on RTX 3060 12 GB · Ryzen 5 5600X · 32 GB DDR4 (ComfyUI 0.37.1)\n\n| This workflow, 2048×2048 (Comfy Desktop, SageAttention on) | Time per image |\n|---|---|\n| QUALITY · 40 steps · Comfy Kitchen attention | **4 min 07 s** |\n| TURBO · Viggle 6-step · SageAttention (Desktop default) | **47 s** |\n\nFirst run after starting ComfyUI adds a few seconds for loading (4 min 11 s / 48 s).\n\nFrom my benchmark (2048×2048, same seed): template 25 steps with PyTorch attention **3 min 57 s** ·\nComfy Kitchen attention **2 min 40 s** · SageAttention **3 min 00 s** · bf16 model **6 min 10 s**.\n\n**Why 40 steps:** at 2K the template's 25 steps left the subject faded on one of my test prompts; 40 steps (the official 40–50) fixed it.\n**TURBO:** much faster, but visibly softer fine detail at 2K than the base model.\n**Seeds vary:** of my two test seeds, TURBO double-exposed the player's head on one, and QUALITY printed the date line twice on one. Re-roll the seed if you see that.\n**Don't add Comfy Kitchen attention to TURBO:** with the 6-step LoRA it ghosted the subject in my test — PyTorch and SageAttention were clean.\n**Text encoder:** `qwen3vl_8b_w4a8` runs at the same speed but changes the picture with the same seed — int8 kept.\n"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## How to use\n\n1. **Step 1** — models are set (int8 = best fit for 12 GB).\n2. **Step 2** — size. Default **4 MP = 2048×2048** (Qwen 2.1's native 2K). 1 MP = 1024×1024.\n3. **Step 3** — write your prompt. cfg stays **1** (negative prompt is unused at cfg 1).\n4. **Run.** QUALITY is on; TURBO is bypassed. To switch: click a group title → **Ctrl+B**.\n\n## Tested on RTX 3060 12 GB · Ryzen 5 5600X · 32 GB DDR4 (ComfyUI 0.37.1)\n\n| This workflow, 2048×2048 (Comfy Desktop, SageAttention on) | Time per image |\n|---|---|\n| QUALITY · 40 steps · Comfy Kitchen attention | **4 min 07 s** |\n| TURBO · Viggle 6-step · SageAttention (Desktop default) | **47 s** |\n\nFirst run after starting ComfyUI adds a few seconds for loading (4 min 11 s / 48 s).\n\nFrom my benchmark (2048×2048, same seed): template 25 steps with PyTorch attention **3 min 57 s** ·\nComfy Kitchen attention **2 min 40 s** · SageAttention **3 min 00 s** · bf16 model **6 min 10 s**.\n\n**Why 40 steps:** at 2K the template's 25 steps left the subject faded on one of my test prompts; 40 steps (the official 40–50) fixed it.\n**TURBO:** much faster, but visibly softer fine detail at 2K than the base model.\n**Seeds vary:** of my two test seeds, TURBO double-exposed the player's head on one, and QUALITY printed the date line twice on one. Re-roll the seed if you see that.\n**Don't add Comfy Kitchen attention to TURBO:** with the 6-step LoRA it ghosted the subject in my test — PyTorch and SageAttention were clean.\n**Text encoder:** `qwen3vl_8b_w4a8` runs at the same speed but changes the picture with the same seed — int8 kept.\n"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
